	"_comment": "The incremental swipe step rule of _shared/lua/gestures/incremental.lua, replayed by the macOS and Linux suites through that module and by the Windows suite through its port (windows/modules/gestures/incremental.ahk). Distances and steps are millimetres of travel along the swipe axis. steps = 0 below the first step (the smaller of first_step and the slot's step), then 1 + floor((distance - first) / step). reverse_min is how far a swipe must come back from its last action to reverse: the larger of the engine floor and half the first step. invalid lists inputs every consumer must refuse; non-finite numbers, which JSON cannot carry, are each consumer's own test.",
